Routing vs Sequential vs Hierarchical

| Arrangement         | Meaning                           | Example                                     |
| ------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| **🌳 Hierarchical** | One main agent manages sub-agents | Main Agent → Sales/Marketing/Finance Agents |
| **➡️ Sequential**   | Agents work one after another     | Research → Analysis → Report                |
| **🚦 Routing**      | Request goes to the correct agent | Sales Question → Sales Agent                |


========

Easy memory trick 🧠
🌳 Hierarchical = Who manages whom

➡️ Sequential = What happens next

🚦 Routing = Where should this request go?

In simple words: Routing = Selecting the correct path or agent for a particular task.

